"""IB DP History (previous guide, last assessment May 2027) – ib-g12-history.

Year 2 of the two-year course: Prescribed Subject 3 "The move to global war" (Japanese expansion in East
Asia 1931–1941; German and Italian expansion 1933–1940), Paper 1 source skills, World History Topics 11
(Causes and effects of 20th-century wars) and 12 (The Cold War), the HL regional option History of Asia
and Oceania (China and Korea 1910–1950, the PRC 1949–2005, South Asia after 1947), Paper 2/3 essay
writing and the Historical Investigation (IA, 2,200 words, 25 marks).

Item styles
  * C1 – define / identify / state (short and MCQ recall of people, dates, terms),
  * C2 – explain / distinguish / correct a misconception,
  * C3 – case-based explanation and Paper 1 source work: Q1(a) comprehension, Q1(b) message of a
    (visual) source, Q2 value and limitations with reference to origin, purpose and content,
  * C4 – Paper 1 Q3 compare and contrast, Q4 "using the sources and your own knowledge", and Paper 2 /
    Paper 3 essays (to what extent / evaluate / discuss / compare and contrast) with markbands.
Source extracts are attributed to real authors and documents; they are paraphrased or adapted and are
labelled as such. Descriptions of visual sources (cartoons, posters, photographs) describe real images.

Mock = one previous-guide HL paper set (14 items, 159 marks):
  Paper 1 (1 h, 24 marks): Q1(a) 3 + Q1(b) 2 + Q2 4 + Q3 6 + Q4 9,
  Paper 2 (1 h 30): four essay prompts from different topics, candidates answer two (15 marks each),
  Paper 3 HL (2 h 30): five regional essay prompts, candidates answer three (15 marks each).
"""
